isks affecting hemostasis.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"盐酸米诺环素 has a defined indication but is vulnerable to cation-mediated absorption loss\",\n            \"explanation\": \"盐酸米诺环素 is indicated for the treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (AECOPD), as supported by clinical documentation [Data: Relationships (23560)]. However, its effectiveness is highly dependent on adequate gastrointestinal absorption, which is markedly reduced when taken with drugs containing multivalent cations (Al³⁺, Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, Fe²⁺/³⁺). These form non-absorbable complexes with the tetracycline backbone of 米诺环素, leading to subtherapeutic concentrations and potential treatment failure [Data: Relationships (45999)]. This interaction exemplifies a well-established class effect among tetracyclines and reinforces the need for patient education on proper administration timing relative to supplements or antacids.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a moderate-to-high clinical impact due to multiple high-severity drug–drug interactions that can lead to therapeutic failure, toxicity, or bleeding complications if not properly managed.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782121947, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1585, "prompt_tokens": 4863, "total_tokens": 6448, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Bile Acid Sequestrants and Related Drug Interactions\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on bile acid sequestrant drugs—particularly 考来替泊 (colestipol) and 